meta {
  name: Refund order (gated)
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{internal_base}}/internal/orders/{{order_id}}/refund
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{service_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Support ticket #123: user paid twice for the same plan",
    "source": "agent:support-triage"
  }
}

docs {
  The gated refund from docs/AGENT_PLAN.md:

    order.amountCents <= refund_auto_approve_ceiling_cents (Setting, default
    1000 = $10)  -> refunds immediately through core's refundOrder(): state
    machine enforced, RESERVED stock released, promo use returned, balance
    credited under the idempotent ledger key `refund:<orderId>`. Responds 200
    { status: "REFUNDED", refundedCents } and publishes `order.refunded` to
    tgshop:events:orders.

    above the ceiling -> mutates nothing; records ONE pending-approval
    AuditLog row (action="order.refund_requested") for a human ADMIN and
    responds 202 { status: "PENDING_APPROVAL", amountCents, ceilingCents,
    alreadyPending }.

  Retry-safe end to end: an already-REFUNDED order answers 200 with
  alreadyRefunded=true instead of an error, and repeat above-ceiling requests
  do not duplicate the pending-approval entry.

  404 for an unknown order id; 409 ORDER_STATE when the order's status has no
  legal edge to REFUNDED (e.g. a PENDING order that was never paid).

  Refunds always land on the internal balance — reversing the original rail
  (Stars, chain transfer) stays a manual, provider-specific admin operation.
}
